msgstr "HISTORIQUE"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
#: opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "POSIX.1-2001, 4.4BSD."
msgstr "POSIX.1-2001, 4.4BSD."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
#: opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"B<socketpair>()  first appeared in 4.2BSD.  It is generally portable to/from "
"non-BSD systems supporting clones of the BSD socket layer (including "
"System\\ V variants)."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<socketpair>() est apparue dans 4.2BSD. Elle est généralement "
"portable de/vers les systèmes non-BSD prenant en charge les clones des "
"sockets BSD (y compris les variantes de System V)."

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Since Linux 2.6.27, B<socketpair>()  supports the B<SOCK_NONBLOCK> and "
"B<SOCK_CLOEXEC> flags in the I<type> argument, as described in B<socket>(2)."
msgstr ""
"Depuis Linux 2.6.27, B<socketpair>() prend en charge les attributs "
"B<SOCK_NONBLOCK> et B<SOCK_CLOEXEC> dans l'argument I<type>, comme décrit "
"dans B<socket>(2)."

